@@ PE6 | Hybrid
A stakeholder demands weekly metrics that the project does not currently track. Collecting them would take significant effort. What should the project manager do?
A) Understand the purpose of the request and agree a cost-effective way to meet it
B) Start collecting all requested metrics immediately, whatever the effort required
C) Refuse the request, since the metrics are not in the communications plan
D) Provide estimated figures without telling the stakeholder they are estimates
= A
? Exploring the underlying need allows a proportionate solution; providing made-up figures would be dishonest.

@@ PE6 | Agile
At a sprint review, insurance agents complain that the new claims screen needs more clicks than the old system. What should the product owner do?
A) Thank them, explore the problem with them and add improvements to the backlog
B) Explain that the new screen follows the approved design, so it cannot change now
C) Ask the agents to put their complaints in writing to the steering committee first
D) Promise to fix every complaint in the next sprint, whatever else is planned
= A
? Feedback at reviews is valuable. The product owner explores it with users and turns it into backlog items that are prioritised against other work.

@@ PE6 | Predictive
The local community expected the mining project to hire local workers, but the contractor has hired mostly from outside the region. Tension is rising. What should the project manager do?
A) Engage the community, review commitments and work on local hiring
